From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4: dense MXFP8 decode GEMM for M 1-192

VLLM_DSV41_DENSE_MXFP8_DECODE (default 0). Dense MXFP8 projections (Marlin 8-bit layout,
e8m0 group-32) read by our CUDA kernels (native/dsv41_dense_mxfp8, built into the image
as vllm/_dsv41_dense_mxfp8.so): warp stream-K for M <= 8, split-K for M 9-64 (CTA-shared
activations, static split-K + fixed-order sum), wide split-K for M 65-192. A measured
per-shape dispatch table enables a kernel only where it beat Marlin by >= 3 %
at both ends of its M range; everything else (other M, bias, scale bytes
outside [1,134]) keeps Marlin. fp64 error at Marlin's level (mean ratio
1.00000-1.00001, max <= 1.0024), not bitwise; deterministic, graph safe.
Layer sequence (8 layers x 5 projections) 1.08-1.29x vs Marlin.

